{"type":"message","id":"80180e78","parentId":"2ae2eb2e","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:12:12.337Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Task Analysis and Plan of Action\n\nTo implement AI analysis for 'Meta Description' in SEOIndicator.com using Test-Driven Development (TDD), I will break the task into the following steps:\n\n---\n\n#### **1. Automated Test Creation:**\n   - Write test cases based on requirements for analyzing meta descriptions:\n     - Check for meta description length compliance (e.g., within the recommended 50–160 characters range).\n     - Identify whether the description contains target keywords.\n     - Analyze whether the description is engaging and provides a good summary.\n     - Detect duplicate or missing meta descriptions.\n\n#### **2. Feature Development:**\n   - Build the feature to pass the tests:\n     - Integrate or train the AI model responsible for analyzing meta descriptions.\n     - Implement the logic for detecting length, keyword usage, engagement, and duplicate/missing issues.\n\n#### **3. Validation of Tests:**\n   - Confirm that all tests pass locally using the created feature.\n   - Adjust tests or refactor code as needed to meet TDD objectives.\n\n#### **4. Git Workflow:**\n   - Create a new branch for the implementation (e.g., `feature/meta-description-ai-analysis`).\n   - Commit changes incrementally (e.g., tests, feature implementation, bug fixes).\n   - Push the branch and create a pull request for integration.\n\n---\n\nI will now start by creating the test cases."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ApNFrCnIi5grSvL7N3DNeE1W","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"tests/test_meta_description_ai.py","content":"import unittest\nfrom meta_description_analyzer import MetaDescriptionAnalyzer\n\nclass TestMetaDescriptionAnalyzer(unittest.TestCase):\n\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.analyzer = MetaDescriptionAnalyzer()\n\n    def test_meta_description_length_valid(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that a meta description within the valid length is recognized as valid.\"\"\"\n        description = \"This is a sample meta description that fits the length requirements.\"\n        result = self.analyzer.analyze_length(description)\n        self.assertTrue(result['is_valid'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_length_invalid(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that a too-short or too-long meta description is flagged as invalid.\"\"\"\n        short_description = \"Too short\"\n        long_description = \"L\" * 300  # Over 160 characters\n        result_short = self.analyzer.analyze_length(short_description)\n        result_long = self.analyzer.analyze_length(long_description)\n        self.assertFalse(result_short['is_valid'])\n        self.assertFalse(result_long['is_valid'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_keyword_usage(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that target keywords are detected in the description.\"\"\"\n        description = \"This is a sample meta description with the keyword SEO.\"\n        keywords = [\"SEO\"]\n        result = self.analyzer.analyze_keywords(description, keywords)\n        self.assertTrue(result['keywords_present'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_engagement(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that the analysis can detect engaging descriptions.\"\"\"\n        description = (\"Discover the top 10 tips for boosting your website's traffic with these simple yet effective SEO strategies.\")\n        result = self.analyzer.analyze_engagement(description)\n        self.assertTrue(result['is_engaging'])\n\n    def test_meta_description_duplicates(self):\n        \"\"\"Test that duplicate or missing meta descriptions are identified.\"\"\"\n        descriptions = [\n            \"Sample meta description 1\",\n            \"Sample meta description 2\",\n            \"Sample meta description 1\",  # Duplicate\n            \"\"  # Missing\n        ]\n        result = self.analyzer.detect_duplicates_and_missing(descriptions)\n        self.assertEqual(result['duplicates'], [\"Sample meta description 1\"])\n        self.assertTrue(result['has_missing'])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-4o","usage":{"input":6125,"output":830,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6955,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770912723294}}
