{"type":"message","id":"c0c10c90","parentId":"1ab03675","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:12:18.991Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"### Automated Test Suite Created\n\nThe test file `test_meta_description_ai.py` is complete. It includes the following test cases:\n1. **`test_meta_description_length_valid`**: Checks that a meta description within the valid range (50-160 chars) is valid.\n2. **`test_meta_description_length_invalid`**: Verifies that too-short/long descriptions are flagged as invalid.\n3. **`test_meta_description_keyword_usage`**: Detects if specified keywords exist in the description.\n4. **`test_meta_description_engagement`**: Analyzes if the description is engaging.\n5. **`test_meta_description_duplicates`**: Identifies duplicate or missing meta descriptions.\n\n---\n\nNext, I will proceed to develop the feature implementations to pass these tests."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_TkphlTOM1cbWoNDqdT14T7pj","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"meta_description_analyzer.py","content":"class MetaDescriptionAnalyzer:\n    def analyze_length(self, description):\n        \"\"\"Analyzes if the meta description length is within the valid range.\"\"\"\n        min_length = 50\n        max_length = 160\n        is_valid = min_length <= len(description) <= max_length\n        return {\n            'is_valid': is_valid,\n            'length': len(description)\n        }\n\n    def analyze_keywords(self, description, keywords):\n        \"\"\"Checks for the presence of target keywords in the description.\"\"\"\n        keywords_present = any(keyword.lower() in description.lower() for keyword in keywords)\n        return {\n            'keywords_present': keywords_present,\n            'keywords_found': [keyword for keyword in keywords if keyword.lower() in description.lower()]\n        }\n\n    def analyze_engagement(self, description):\n        \"\"\"Analyzes if the description is engaging. Placeholder logic for now.\"\"\"\n        # In a real implementation, this could call an AI model for sentiment analysis or engagement prediction.\n        # For simplicity, consider the description engaging if it has over 10 words and ends with a call to action or a period.\n        is_engaging = len(description.split()) > 10 and description.strip().endswith(('.', '!'))\n        return {\n            'is_engaging': is_engaging\n        }\n\n    def detect_duplicates_and_missing(self, descriptions):\n        \"\"\"Detects duplicate and missing meta descriptions.\"\"\"\n        seen = set()\n        duplicates = set()\n        has_missing = False\n\n        for description in descriptions:\n            if not description.strip():\n                has_missing = True\n            elif description in seen:\n                duplicates.add(description)\n            else:\n                seen.add(description)\n\n        return {\n            'duplicates': list(duplicates),\n            'has_missing': has_missing\n        }"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"github-copilot","model":"gpt-4o","usage":{"input":576,"output":594,"cacheRead":6400,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":7570,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770912732388}}
